[{:db/id "q-31163/selection/498842c7bc10e2aebeca4e943353a7ad2a2c27fb13fa7174a7d1d3a6386ab377" :answer/id #uuid "476c6d00-be94-525a-894a-65cbdc6739c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11-2x)-9{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31163/selection/148c59ebf271cf13f2c6c27c45a7639d553efde5085a18fe60a40d380cfcc313" :answer/id #uuid "12305e26-6a25-5c6d-810e-b9d752269023" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11-2x)-18{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31163/selection/0ecd7220544df4f6dcc01e134f616dfb8e4ae08a3d9e642c2d515c2911d90eb5" :answer/id #uuid "c97683d2-8e12-524c-8411-b23e88ede341" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11-2x)-9{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31163/selection/d96ffb60d2772acbbf59b9818d70797ca5e85bc76effd35a566bc2cfbfa468f9" :answer/id #uuid "a445d0d3-e28c-5b06-91d1-143b05f19bac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11-2x)-18{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31163/selection/962f94574b6888513390c3028b92497f487d56943d4409a508a828859953f797" :answer/id #uuid "5c7028e6-fa2e-574b-bc01-412f1172e3a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11-2x)-18{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31163/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26b8fb54-5311-5364-bd5c-960c7033a62f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31163/selection/962f94574b6888513390c3028b92497f487d56943d4409a508a828859953f797" :answer-field/choices ["q-31163/selection/498842c7bc10e2aebeca4e943353a7ad2a2c27fb13fa7174a7d1d3a6386ab377" "q-31163/selection/148c59ebf271cf13f2c6c27c45a7639d553efde5085a18fe60a40d380cfcc313" "q-31163/selection/0ecd7220544df4f6dcc01e134f616dfb8e4ae08a3d9e642c2d515c2911d90eb5" "q-31163/selection/d96ffb60d2772acbbf59b9818d70797ca5e85bc76effd35a566bc2cfbfa468f9" "q-31163/selection/962f94574b6888513390c3028b92497f487d56943d4409a508a828859953f797"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31163" :question/id #uuid "893bef04-f620-5797-a1c9-55f06c3838d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-31163" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11-2x)-6{x}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11-2x)$ and $h(x)=-6{x}^{3}.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =g(x)+h(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we differentiate $g(x).$ We express $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11-2x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ng=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u=11-2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11-2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate $h(x)=-6{x}^{3}.$ \n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}=-18{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={g}^{′}(x)+{h}^{′}(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11-2x)-18{x}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31163/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "73216188-6524-55c3-b945-86d13ef64170"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31163"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-310179/field-1/66d4d29e8530fa3ba714197d9bb72783a49714395c98d4b58c1e24d062c777e1" :answer/id #uuid "ec035f43-416c-54c4-bdd9-7691e264d439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12x^3}{\\cos(3x^4-5)^2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-310179/field-1/5d343b06e7736f40023710e95bacc19658307f606d067df6379774ea7410fa31" :answer/id #uuid "82659cf2-0d0d-571c-b677-a9734bdbc77a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12x^3}{\\cos(3x^4-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-310179/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "99c14107-35e5-52c8-83bc-1bf1bfa7db9e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-310179/field-1/66d4d29e8530fa3ba714197d9bb72783a49714395c98d4b58c1e24d062c777e1" :answer-field/choices ["q-310179/field-1/66d4d29e8530fa3ba714197d9bb72783a49714395c98d4b58c1e24d062c777e1" "q-310179/field-1/5d343b06e7736f40023710e95bacc19658307f606d067df6379774ea7410fa31"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-310179" :question/id #uuid "8cfab55f-c242-579e-bda0-8364a79dbcb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-310179" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3{x}^{4}-5)$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as a composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡u,\\,u=3{x}^{4}-5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={sec}^{2}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=12{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot 12{x}^{3} \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}{sec}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}{sec}^{2}⁡(3{x}^{4}-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-310179/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "73216188-6524-55c3-b945-86d13ef64170"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-310179"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31153/selection/dc26275fd6d040df526c8b20bd9bb22c3bff2e63c845a76e13fccd34ccaa3caf" :answer/id #uuid "6dc70b98-d298-59c7-938c-cc7c651b0ea8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31153/selection/ed62400941791598b5d2cf6b8bd8274885180c4334a548162e0b16fba5232d2c" :answer/id #uuid "c05fb58d-9abe-58c1-af56-6ca076f3b64a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31153/selection/ec533a49f521c51e771dc3969490c4e7235ec9067435ed74f9e917a045913cc9" :answer/id #uuid "36261555-c139-5597-a434-0b8bd0c91c4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31153/selection/41c8a8ce3fc9583cd0e7f6e9f901a20e683236be911caa5e76aa522e52c65d63" :answer/id #uuid "76fd204e-60e7-5ff5-9218-21d79e5b7a9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31153/selection/6a119a8fbb6dc3be745162c21b42edb592d807b8d97e55fdda355d479a9c093f" :answer/id #uuid "3f17b977-aa51-5d8b-aee8-90db30dbda49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31153/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fe8829f-3848-511c-aeb8-9a5d23803897" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31153/selection/dc26275fd6d040df526c8b20bd9bb22c3bff2e63c845a76e13fccd34ccaa3caf" :answer-field/choices ["q-31153/selection/dc26275fd6d040df526c8b20bd9bb22c3bff2e63c845a76e13fccd34ccaa3caf" "q-31153/selection/ed62400941791598b5d2cf6b8bd8274885180c4334a548162e0b16fba5232d2c" "q-31153/selection/ec533a49f521c51e771dc3969490c4e7235ec9067435ed74f9e917a045913cc9" "q-31153/selection/41c8a8ce3fc9583cd0e7f6e9f901a20e683236be911caa5e76aa522e52c65d63" "q-31153/selection/6a119a8fbb6dc3be745162c21b42edb592d807b8d97e55fdda355d479a9c093f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31153" :question/id #uuid "e330e01e-de68-56a1-a720-c5093ac56875" :question/math-academy-id "q-31153" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)$ at the point where $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=2$ is given by ${f}^{′}(2).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,u=3x+5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=2,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 2+5) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡11.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=2$ is $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡11.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31153/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "73216188-6524-55c3-b945-86d13ef64170"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31153"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-310180/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "6d5e87b6-f630-5904-b169-dff4595b1ae7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-310180/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "b5937a9f-fc76-5f26-945c-920b1984b07e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-310180/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "16a10934-9000-5467-9780-1c375d10c554" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-310180/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-310180/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-310180/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-310180" :question/id #uuid "f6e54a0b-e178-5c73-9eda-94e5c3fac631" :question/math-academy-id "q-310180" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is given by ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,u=3x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is \n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-310180/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "73216188-6524-55c3-b945-86d13ef64170"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-310180"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-51026/selection/93ce1375ed01e4d84c40a88e58ef609b1c760d0475cd275a0163b9524f1b90a9" :answer/id #uuid "d0d23b72-d731-5471-b74f-b9ad4bb4648c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2x+2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51026/selection/dcf45848fada9bd0d3da972450bf70aadfa00929c76443c78f0501e01e295f17" :answer/id #uuid "03a18169-8bbb-5b45-8963-cdb629b604d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x+\\pi -2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51026/selection/0ce7cf8a31709eb718ecea574a0cf6f419e47d63f82b6b93a2e6b1a07501e16c" :answer/id #uuid "d73f56b1-72e9-57a6-8bcc-057cd05ae84f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x-\\pi -3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51026/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer/id #uuid "ea6d7c03-57ab-5d89-83fb-8d4d2fc62d00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51026/selection/f5d98a631ee48ed70accf24f8b6cebcd32363395da4e87feeaf883d85b9bc131" :answer/id #uuid "a0b57ff7-acb7-5f51-9f0e-e35a8da46dd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51026/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "29d65b6f-1e64-5150-a3a7-70e1c80995c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-51026/selection/f5d98a631ee48ed70accf24f8b6cebcd32363395da4e87feeaf883d85b9bc131" :answer-field/choices ["q-51026/selection/93ce1375ed01e4d84c40a88e58ef609b1c760d0475cd275a0163b9524f1b90a9" "q-51026/selection/dcf45848fada9bd0d3da972450bf70aadfa00929c76443c78f0501e01e295f17" "q-51026/selection/0ce7cf8a31709eb718ecea574a0cf6f419e47d63f82b6b93a2e6b1a07501e16c" "q-51026/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" "q-51026/selection/f5d98a631ee48ed70accf24f8b6cebcd32363395da4e87feeaf883d85b9bc131"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51026" :question/id #uuid "dac57425-439e-57f2-8c4b-329068ff1544" :question/math-academy-id "q-51026" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)$ at the point $(1+\\pi ,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=1+\\pi $ is given by ${f}^{′}(1+\\pi ).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u=x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=1+\\pi ,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1+\\pi ) & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1+\\pi -1) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at the point $(1+\\pi ,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-2) & =0(x-(1+\\pi )) \\\\ y+2 & =0 \\\\ y & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-51026/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "73216188-6524-55c3-b945-86d13ef64170"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51026"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31320/selection/31cb5faecf97de418537f9d779998337fe008cc4df5271e72c4687c7e42f2d68" :answer/id #uuid "019c222f-c9f3-5a25-a904-8a8c25580cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x-1)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31320/selection/043de0d6e985f83b1c6e8d2f4d770453f777875ec124ccaca284e2a0d854f78b" :answer/id #uuid "dfd75089-4674-5c53-8373-d731852c4d67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x-1)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31320/selection/ae12232e93c498579fad790d7d84b7d0aeaa4dc7c065a6cd0809107ab9054d8e" :answer/id #uuid "cc7c88df-be7b-58ec-bcd7-31051e196f1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2x-1)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31320/selection/59ac280c16675803d3e14218c9d95680fcb3eb0e21df3f9b